Z||000000||Alex2004||01-21-2001||10:04 PM||||I just thought i'd let you all know since i posted a topic asking how to do them before. I wired them to the parking lights because that was an easy way to do it. . Since we put the fast back on and my car is an 84, the amber lights wouldn't work, and there were Brake/parking sockets on each side, and we only needed 2. And so i just used the brown parking light wire on one of the spare sockets and used these little blue splice clamp connector deals and and then used the second PONTIAC hot wire on one of the usable sockets. Then i put all 4 negative wires and tied them together and put an eye connector on them and screwed it to the frame. I love the way it looks at night!!!! I'll post a pic sometime just to show you my accomplishments! LOL. I am hoping to get my 3rd brake light installed soon. I just need the plug that the bulb/socket plugs into. Well just though i'd let you guys know....<BR>Alex...<P>||||reg||10
